[Official waste management reference]
Wet or biodegradable waste includes food scraps, fruit peels, and vegetable waste. These streams are suitable for composting or municipal wet-waste collection.

[Official waste management reference]
Dry or recyclable waste includes paper, cardboard, plastics, and tins. These items should be cleaned where possible and stored separately for recycling.

[Official waste management reference]
Used batteries, electronic devices, and other hazardous waste should not be disposed of in ordinary household waste. They require special collection or authorized handling routes.

[Official waste management reference]
When official guidance is not available or the item is uncertain, households should verify instructions with the local municipal authority before disposal.

